+- **Real product editing — name, country, tier, and every other field can now be changed after
+  creation, not just price, stock, and photo.** The backend already fully supported this
+  (`PATCH /products/:id` genuinely accepted every field); only the frontend UI was missing.
+  Deliberately built to avoid a real data-loss risk: the edit form doesn't touch fields it has no
+  real control over (a product's curated flavor profile, brew guide, or moment match), so fixing
+  a typo in the name can't silently blank out hand-tuned data the way a from-scratch rebuild of
+  those fields would have. A new Playwright test confirms an edit genuinely reflects on the real
+  public Shop page. See Tier 1 for full detail.
